{%- comment -%}
  Horizontal lifestyle strip under the product grid.

  Source geometry (measured on the live page with slick running): cells are FLUID, not fixed.
  The scroller keeps a 50px peek on each side and every cell is
  `(trackWidth - 100) / slidesToShow` wide. Inside a cell the image is inset 4px left and
  20px right, so neighbours sit 24px apart. Arrows are tall translucent side bars, 51px wide,
  with an orange angle glyph.

  slidesToShow steps at 770 and 993, not 769 and 992: slick's mobileFirst compares
  `window.innerWidth > breakpoint`, so a 992px window still gets the 769 tier. The page
  padding steps on the CSS breakpoints (inclusive), which is why a 769px window shows the
  32px-tier inset with the 1.5-up ladder.

  The loop follows the same 770 boundary: infinite above it (so a slice of the previous image
  always shows at rest), finite below, where the arrows hide at each end.

  Vertical rhythm is viewport-independent and comes from the section, not the cells: 64px
  above (48 section padding + 16 on the gallery wrapper) and 48px below (16 + the banner's
  32). The track's 7.4px bottom pad reproduces the descender slack the source gets for free
  from laying its cells out as inline-block in a 22.4px line box; drop it if that changes.
  Cell HEIGHT is derived, not fixed — the art is square, so it follows cell width.

  Images match the source's fill mode: width 100%, height auto, object-fit fill. With height
  auto the box already carries the file's own ratio, so nothing crops and nothing letterboxes;
  a non-square file just makes its cell taller or shorter instead. The width/height attributes
  come from the file so the reserved space matches and the row does not shift on load.

  Data: pdp.feature_carousel (list.file), and nothing else — a product with no images in
  that metafield renders no section at all, rather than standing in product shots.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign p = product
  if p == blank and request.visual_preview_mode
    assign p = collections.all.products.first
  endif
  assign shots = p.metafields.pdp.feature_carousel.value
  assign limit = section.settings.max_images | default: 8
-%}

{%- comment -%} Metafield only: no images set means no strip at all {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if shots != blank and shots.size > 0 -%}
  {%- assign items = shots -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if items != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The row bleeds 15px past the container on BOTH sides, so the inset is the page padding
    minus 15: measured live at 1/1, 17/17, 41/41, 57/57. It is container-FLUID — no max width,
    so at 1800 the cells keep growing instead of centring in a 1440 box. The inset also sets
    the track width every cell divides, so getting it wrong shifts every cell by
    15/slidesToShow. Inset lives here; the 50px peek lives on the scroller.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="spy-strip mt-16 mb-12 px-px min-[769px]:px-[17px] min-[1200px]:px-[41px] min-[1800px]:px-[57px]"
    {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- comment -%} Arrows anchor to the track, not the padded shell — the source puts them at -1px {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      # Endless at every width, arrows from 993px up. JSON lives in an assign: Shopify cuts {{ }} at the first brace
      assign strip_opts = '{"speed":300,"step":1,"loop":1,"arrows":[0,0,1],"bp":[769,992]}'
    -%}
    <spy-slider class="relative block" data-opts="{{ strip_opts | escape }}">
      {%- comment -%}
        display via square brackets because Horizon's base.css owns the .flex class name and
        adds a 14.4px gap. px-[50px] is slick's centerPadding: it makes the peek, and it also
        shrinks the percentage basis below so a cell matches slick's slideWidth exactly.
        Keep comments outside the tag — a whitespace-trimming comment tag eats the newline
        after "<div" and glues the tag name onto the class attribute.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        class="spy-strip__track [display:flex] snap-x snap-mandatory overflow-x-auto px-[50px] pb-[7.4px] scroll-pl-[50px] [--spy-show:1.5] min-[770px]:[--spy-show:3] min-[993px]:[--spy-show:4] [scrollbar-width:none] [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden"
        data-track
      >
        {%- for img in items limit: limit -%}
          {%- comment -%} 4px left / 20px right, the way the source's p-1 + padding-right stack up {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="spy-strip__cell shrink-0 basis-[calc(100%_/_var(--spy-show))] snap-start py-1 pl-1 pr-5">
            <img
              src="{{ img | image_url: width: 800 }}"
              srcset="{{ img | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ img | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ img | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
              sizes="(min-width: 992px) 25vw, (min-width: 769px) 33vw, 50vw"
              alt="{{ img.alt | default: p.title | escape }}"
              width="{{ img.width | default: 1200 }}"
              height="{{ img.height | default: 1200 }}"
              loading="lazy"
              class="block h-auto w-full bg-white object-fill"
            >
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Site-wide carousel arrow (QA, 9 Nov): 40px white circle with an orange chevron,
        centred on the strip, in place of the source's full-height white bars.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'spy-slider-arrow', dir: 'prev', class: 'absolute left-[5px] top-1/2 z-[2] -translate-y-1/2' -%}
      {%- render 'spy-slider-arrow', dir: 'next', class: 'absolute right-[5px] top-1/2 z-[2] -translate-y-1/2' -%}
    </spy-slider>
  </div>

  <script src="{{ 'spy-slider.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SPY Lifestyle Carousel",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Images come from the product metafield pdp.feature_carousel. With none set the section does not render. Source art is square, 1200x1200."
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "max_images", "label": "Images", "min": 3, "max": 12, "step": 1, "default": 8 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "SPY Lifestyle Carousel" }]
}
{% endschema %}
